    "consulting_editor": "Erin E. Runcan •Ovulation induction may be attempted once cytology reaches >70% anucleated cells and follicles are >4–5 mm (toy to small-breed canine), 5–7 mm (medium to large-breed canine), 7–10 mm (giant-breed canine), or 2–3 mm (feline). •Ovulation-inducing agents: ◦ GnRH: 1.1–2.2μg/kg IM or IV; 25μg/cat IM; may repeat daily for 1–3 days in bitches, single dose for queens. ◦ Human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG): 500–1,000 IU/dog IM; 500 IU/queen IM; may repeat in 2–3 days if ovulation does not occur. ◦ GnRH and hCG may be given concurrently or alternating days. ◦ Deslorelin implant (2.1 mg implant— Ovuplant® or 4.7 mg implant—Suprelorin®) placed subcutaneously. If breeding and ovulation is confirmed (progesterone >10 ng/mL), implant should be removed. If not breeding, leave implant in place. ◦ In queens, cervical stimulation may be performed from initial induction several times daily for 24–48 hours. FOLLOW-UP MISCELLANEOUS canine estrous cycles. Theriogenology 2007, 68:1205–1210.",
